-- title:
--   A probability-valued balanced experiment at every sample size
-- statement:
--   For a true mixing law \(G_\star\) on \(K\subseteq\mathbb R^d\), define
--   \[
--   \bar r_{d,n}=\left(\frac{\log n}{\log\log n}\right)^d+\log n,\qquad
--   \alpha_{d,n}=\bar r_{d,n}\log n.
--   \]
--   Use the effective shape \(\widetilde\alpha_{d,n}=\alpha_{d,n}\) when
--   \(\alpha_{d,n}>0\), and \(\widetilde\alpha_{d,n}=1\) otherwise. The balanced experiment is the independent product of the \(n\)-sample Gaussian-mixture law and \(n\) Gamma laws with shape and rate \(\widetilde\alpha_{d,n}\). The included probability-measure instance establishes that this is a probability law for every sample size. The fallback at nonpositive shapes leaves the eventual balanced regime unchanged.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianJointConsistency.lean#L17-L35

